{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NmnQVLDBRhQHTrjKk5DTsR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Register functions as methods of Pandas DataFrame and Series.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\timport warnings\n6\tfrom functools import wraps\n7\t\n8\tfrom pandas.core.groupby.generic import DataFrameGroupBy\n9\tfrom pandas.util._exceptions import find_stack_level\n10\tfrom pandas.api.extensions import (\n11\t    register_series_accessor,\n12\t    register_dataframe_accessor,\n13\t)\n14\timport inspect\n15\t\n16\tmethod_call_ctx_factory = None\n17\t\n18\t\n19\tdef handle_pandas_extension_call(method, method_signature, obj, args, kwargs):\n20\t    \"\"\"Handle pandas extension call.\n21\t\n22\t    This function is called when the user calls\n23\t    a pandas DataFrame object's method.\n24\t    The pandas extension mechanism passes args and kwargs\n25\t    of the original method call as it is applied to obj.\n26\t\n27\t    Our implementation uses the global variable `method_call_ctx_factory`.\n28\t\n29\t    `method_call_ctx_factory` can be either None or an abstract class.\n30\t\n31\t    When `method_call_ctx_factory` is None,\n32\t    the implementation calls the registered method\n33\t    with unmodified args and kwargs and returns underlying method result.\n34\t\n35\t    When `method_call_ctx_factory` is not None,\n36\t    `method_call_ctx_factory` is expected to refer to\n37\t    the function to create the context object.\n38\t    The context object will be used to process\n39\t    inputs and outputs of `method` calls.\n40\t    It is also possible that\n41\t    the context object method `handle_start_method_call`\n42\t    will modify original args and kwargs before `method` call.\n43\t\n44\t    `method_call_ctx_factory` is a function\n45\t    that should have the following signature:\n46\t\n47\t     `f(method_name: str, args: list, kwargs: dict) -> MethodCallCtx`\n48\t\n49\t\n50\t    MethodCallCtx is